---
title: "Implemented Data Flow (as-built, verified by live testing)"
---

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant CLI as aqe CLI<br/>(Cobra)
    participant DC as docling/<br/>client.go
    participant D as Docling<br/>:5001
    participant CH as chunker/<br/>chunker.go
    participant PY as chunk_helper.py
    participant WC as search/<br/>weaviate.go
    participant W as Weaviate<br/>:8080
    participant O as Ollama<br/>:11434
    participant CC as claude/<br/>wrapper.go
    participant CL as claude CLI
    participant H as harvard/<br/>harvard_us.go
    participant S as store/<br/>sqlite.go
    participant DB as quotes.db

    Note over U,DB: INGEST PHASE (aqe ingest path --title T --author A --year Y)

    U->>CLI: aqe ingest paper.pdf --title ... --author ... --year ...
    CLI->>CLI: getFilesToIngest(path)<br/>filter .pdf/.docx/.txt/.md

    loop For each file
        CLI->>S: CalculateChecksum(file) [SHA-256]
        CLI->>S: GetDocumentByChecksum()
        S->>DB: SELECT ... WHERE checksum = ?
        alt Already ingested
            DB-->>S: existing record
            S-->>CLI: skip duplicate
        else New document
            DB-->>S: nil
            CLI->>DC: ConvertFile(ctx, filePath)
            DC->>D: POST /v1/convert/file [multipart]
            Note right of D: Parses PDF layout,<br/>extracts text items,<br/>metadata, tables
            D-->>DC: DoclingDocument JSON
            DC-->>CLI: *DoclingDocument

            alt Python chunker available
                CLI->>CH: ChunkDocument(ctx, docJSON)
                CH->>PY: stdin: DoclingDocument JSON
                Note right of PY: HierarchicalChunker<br/>(no token/overlap config)
                PY-->>CH: stdout: JSON lines (id, text, page, section, bbox)
                CH-->>CLI: []ChunkOutput
            else Chunker unavailable (fallback)
                Note over CLI: [DEBUG] Chunker failed,<br/>falling back to text items
                CLI->>CLI: textItemsToChunks(doc, docID)<br/>uses DoclingDocument.Texts directly
            end

            CLI->>S: InsertDocument(doc)
            S->>DB: INSERT INTO documents
            DB-->>S: document ID

            loop For each chunk
                CLI->>WC: InsertChunk(ctx, id, docID, text, page, sections)
                WC->>W: POST object to Chunk class
                W->>O: Auto-embed via text2vec-ollama<br/>(nomic-embed-text, 768 dims)
                O-->>W: embedding vector
                W-->>WC: UUID
                Note right of WC: If insert fails:<br/>continues silently<br/>(debug-only warning)
            end

            CLI->>S: InsertChunks(chunks) [batch]
            S->>DB: INSERT INTO chunks (transaction)
        end
    end

    CLI-->>U: Ingested N documents, M chunks

    Note over U,DB: EXTRACT PHASE (aqe extract topic --max-quotes 20 --min-relevance 60)

    U->>CLI: aqe extract "cultural bias in algorithms"
    CLI->>S: GetChunkCount()
    S->>DB: SELECT count(*) FROM chunks
    alt No chunks
        CLI-->>U: Error: No documents in corpus
    end

    CLI->>WC: HybridSearch(ctx, topic, 50, alpha=0.5)
    WC->>W: GraphQL hybrid query<br/>BM25 + vector, limit 50
    W-->>WC: Top 50 ChunkResults<br/>(text, chunkID, docID, page, score)
    WC-->>CLI: []ChunkResult

    CLI->>CC: ExtractQuotes(ctx, task)
    CC->>CC: buildPrompt(topic, chunks)<br/>via text/template
    CC->>CL: exec: claude --print<br/>--output-format json<br/>-p "prompt" [120s timeout]
    Note right of CL: Scores each chunk 0-100<br/>Returns chunk IDs only<br/>NEVER generates quote text
    CL-->>CC: JSON envelope<br/>{type: "result", result: "..."}
    CC->>CC: Parse outer envelope<br/>Extract result string<br/>Parse inner JSON
    CC-->>CLI: ExtractionResponse<br/>{selected_chunks: [...]}

    CLI->>CLI: Filter: relevance >= min-relevance<br/>Cap at max-quotes

    loop For each selected chunk
        CLI->>S: Raw SQL: JOIN chunks + documents
        Note right of S: Bypasses Store methods,<br/>uses db.DB().QueryRow() directly
        S->>DB: SELECT c.*, d.* WHERE c.id = ?
        DB-->>S: chunk text + document metadata
        CLI->>H: FormatInText(ref)
        H-->>CLI: "(Author, Year)" or "(Author, Year, p. N)"
    end

    CLI->>S: Raw SQL: INSERT INTO extractions
    CLI->>S: Raw SQL: INSERT INTO extracted_quotes [loop]
    S->>DB: INSERT extraction + quotes

    CLI-->>U: Extraction #N: "topic"<br/>Retrieved M quotes (relevance >= 60)<br/>Quote 1 (Relevance: 92/100)<br/>"verbatim text..."<br/> -- (Author, Year)<br/>...<br/>Saved as extraction #N. Export with: aqe export N

    Note over U,DB: LIST PHASE (aqe list)

    U->>CLI: aqe list
    CLI->>S: Raw SQL: SELECT + COUNT GROUP BY
    S->>DB: SELECT extractions with quote counts
    DB-->>S: rows
    CLI-->>U: #1: "topic" - 20 quotes | date<br/>Export: aqe export 1

    Note over U,DB: EXPORT PHASE (aqe export id --format markdown --output file)

    U->>CLI: aqe export 1 --format markdown
    CLI->>S: Raw SQL: SELECT extraction WHERE id = ?
    S->>DB: query
    DB-->>S: extraction record
    CLI->>S: Raw SQL: JOIN extracted_quotes + chunks + documents
    S->>DB: query
    DB-->>S: quotes with full details

    alt format = markdown
        CLI->>H: FormatInText(ref) per quote
        CLI->>H: FormatFull(ref) per unique document
        CLI-->>U: # Quotes: topic<br/>> "verbatim text"<br/>> -- (Author, Year)<br/>> **Relevance (N/100)**: explanation<br/>## Bibliography<br/>Author (Year) *Title*. Publisher.
    else format = json
        CLI->>H: FormatInText + FormatFull per quote
        CLI-->>U: {"extraction": {...}, "quotes": [...]}
    else format = bibtex
        CLI-->>U: @misc{key, author={...}, title={...}, year={...}}
    end

    Note over U,DB: META FIX PHASE (aqe meta fix)

    U->>CLI: aqe meta fix
    CLI->>S: Raw SQL: SELECT documents WHERE title/author/year IS NULL
    S->>DB: query
    DB-->>S: incomplete documents
    loop For each incomplete document
        CLI-->>U: Document: filename<br/>Author: (missing)<br/>Year: (missing)
        U->>CLI: stdin: author name, year
        CLI->>S: Raw SQL: UPDATE documents SET ...
        S->>DB: update
    end
    CLI-->>U: Updated / All documents have complete metadata
